d":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ReactingToChanges"]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A reader is any type you choose to identify the code reading, such as the system’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type. The world keeps each reader’s place in the events, so readers don’t affect one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another, and a copy of the world keeps the places its original had:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum SoundReader {}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Health(current: 3))","let asteroid = world.spawn(Health(current: 1))","world.send(Collision(first: ship, second: asteroid))","","let heard = world.readEvents(Collision.self, by: SoundReader.self)","print(heard.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\"","","let heardAgain = world.readEvents(Collision.self, by: SoundReader.self)","print(heardAgain.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","","let damaging = world.readEvents(Collision.self, by: DamageReader.self)","print(damaging.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A reader that doesn’t read for two updates misses the events dropped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1). The view shares the events’ storage.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/readevents(_:by:)"]}],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/updateEvents()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Ends an update for every event type, dropping the events sent before the previous","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"te